# Profiling and debug logs

For runtime diagnostics in this project, **never** ask the user to copy from the browser console.

Use `profileLogger` through helpers:

- `profileDebug(scope, label, meta?)` — general debug (`src/utils/profileDebug.ts`)
- `profileMark` / `profileAutosave` — projects/autosave (`src/utils/projectProfile.ts`)
- `profileHotkeyAltP` — hotkey tracing (`src/utils/profileHotkeys.ts`)

Logs flush to `profiling/latest.json` in dev (Vite `/__profiling/save`). Read that file in the repo to analyze.

## Profile sets

Rec writes only the **active set** (`localStorage rs:profile:set`, default `save`). Switch in debug overlay: Frame / Save / All.

| Set | What is written |
|---|---|
| `frame` | `video.`, `canvas.`, `draw.`, `values.`, `platformer.`, `frame.` |
| `save` | `projects.` + `canvas.downloadGpu` |
| `all` | everything |

Call sites stay in code. Names are not renamed. Filter is at write time in `ProfileLogger`.

Enable: **Rec** in debug overlay. Optional `localStorage.setItem('rs:profile', '1')` is not required for save spans when Rec is on.

Do not use `console.log` / `console.info` for agent-facing debug output.
